 ## Overview
-This method is the spatial representation component of the KFD-NeRF pipeline, designed to encode canonical 3D points for dynamic neural radiance fields. It solves the problem of balancing high-fidelity 3D reconstruction with computational efficiency and model size, which are critical for dynamic scenes. It sets itself apart from pure MLPs by avoiding convergence difficulties and from multi-scale voxel grids by achieving significantly smaller memory footprints while maintaining comparable or superior rendering quality [S1]. It builds on the TriPlane NeRF representation by adding a specific multi-scale feature aggregation strategy and a two-MLP decoding architecture (Sigma and Color) [S1].
+This method is the spatial representation component of the KFD-NeRF pipeline, designed to encode canonical 3D points for dynamic neural radiance fields [S1]. It solves the problem of balancing high-fidelity 3D reconstruction with computational efficiency and model size, which are critical for dynamic scenes [S1]. It sets itself apart from pure MLPs by avoiding convergence difficulties and from multi-scale voxel grids by achieving significantly smaller memory footprints while maintaining comparable or superior rendering quality [S1]. It builds on the TriPlane NeRF representation by adding a specific multi-scale feature aggregation strategy and a two-MLP decoding architecture (Sigma and Color) [S1].
 
